    {
      "text": "Figure 2: Overview of LLaDA. (a) Pre-training. LLaDA is trained on text with random masks",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        184.13978576660156,
        503.99737548828125,
        193.1658935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "applied independently to all tokens at the same ratio t ∼U[0, 1]. (b) SFT. Only response tokens are",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        194.45101928710938,
        504.01324462890625,
        204.07489013671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "possibly masked. (c) Sampling. LLaDA simulates a diffusion process from t = 1 (fully masked) to",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        205.91896057128906,
        503.9983215332031,
        214.98492431640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "t = 0 (unmasked), predicting all masks simultaneously at each step with flexible remask strategies.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        216.8279571533203,
        502.4591979980469,
        225.8939208984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• The pre-trained LLaDA 8B Base surpasses LLaMA2 7B Base [21] on nearly all 15 standard",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        245.474365234375,
        503.99835205078125,
        254.38092041015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "zero/few-shot learning tasks while performing on par with LLaMA3 8B Base [6], showcasing",
      "bbox": [
        116.46800231933594,
        256.38336181640625,
        503.9963684082031,
        265.2899169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "effective in-context learning capability.",
      "bbox": [
        116.46800231933594,
        267.2923583984375,
        272.1734313964844,
        276.19891357421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• LLaDA significantly enhances the ability to follow instructions after SFT, as demonstrated in case",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        280.141357421875,
        503.99591064453125,
        289.04791259765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "studies such as multi-turn dialogue.",
      "bbox": [
        116.46800231933594,
        291.05035400390625,
        257.87713623046875,
        299.9569091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "• LLaDA effectively breaks the reversal curse [15] with consistent performance across forward and",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        303.89935302734375,
        504.0013732910156,
        312.805908203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reversal tasks. Notably, it outperforms GPT-4o in a reversal poem completion task.",
      "bbox": [
        116.46800231933594,
        314.8093566894531,
        446.1902770996094,
        323.7159118652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        345.3879089355469,
        113.97760009765625,
        356.1356201171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approach",
      "bbox": [
        125.93280029296875,
        345.3879089355469,
        176.56307983398438,
        356.1356201171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this section, we introduce the probabilistic formulation6, along with the pre-training, supervised",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        368.311767578125,
        503.9955139160156,
        378.8069152832031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "fine-tuning, and inference procedures for LLaDA, as illustrated in Fig. 2.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        380.8093566894531,
        398.1208801269531,
        389.7159118652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2.1",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        405.0538024902344,
        120.4532470703125,
        414.01019287109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Probabilistic Formulation",
      "bbox": [
        130.4158477783203,
        405.0538024902344,
        240.41290283203125,
        414.01019287109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Unlike ARMs in Eq. (2), LLaDA defines a model distribution pθ(x0) through a forward process and",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        424.9889831542969,
        503.9991760253906,
        434.7499084472656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a reverse process [16–20]. The forward process gradually masks tokens independently in x0 until",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        435.8979797363281,
        503.99981689453125,
        446.4579162597656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the sequence is fully masked at t = 1. For t ∈(0, 1), the sequence xt is partially masked, with each",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        446.2490539550781,
        504.0027770996094,
        457.3669128417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "being masked with probability t or remaining unmasked with probability 1 −t. The reverse process",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        457.1580505371094,
        503.99896240234375,
        466.78192138671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "recovers the data distribution by iteratively predicting masked tokens as t moves from 1 to 0.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        468.6249694824219,
        477.11431884765625,
        477.69091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The core of LLaDA is a mask predictor, a parametric model pθ(·|xt) that takes xt as input and",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        484.4560546875,
        503.99688720703125,
        495.57391357421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "predicts all masked tokens (denoted as M) simultaneously. It is trained using a cross-entropy loss",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        496.0823669433594,
        503.9974365234375,
        504.9889221191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "computed only on the masked tokens [18–20]:",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        506.9913330078125,
        292.6466979980469,
        515.8978881835938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "L(θ) ≜−Et,x0,xt",
      "bbox": [
        200.01998901367188,
        534.089111328125,
        270.742431640625,
        545.0183715820312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\"",
      "bbox": [
        273.3979797363281,
        524.1265258789062,
        279.2061767578125,
        530.5025634765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "bbox": [
        280.40496826171875,
        527.907958984375,
        285.3862609863281,
        536.7547607421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "t",
      "bbox": [
        281.09698486328125,
        541.48095703125,
        284.6934814453125,
        550.3277587890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "L",
      "bbox": [
        292.7039794921875,
        524.2681884765625,
        298.17144775390625,
        530.4609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "X",
      "bbox": [
        288.2419738769531,
        531.6985473632812,
        302.637939453125,
        538.0745849609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i=1",
      "bbox": [
        288.9839782714844,
        548.4761962890625,
        301.8924865722656,
        554.6689453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1[xi",
      "bbox": [
        304.29296875,
        532.608154296875,
        320.5533752441406,
        543.6431884765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "t = M] log pθ(xi",
      "bbox": [
        317.7359619140625,
        532.608154296875,
        384.245361328125,
        545.9567260742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0|xt)",
      "bbox": [
        381.4279479980469,
        534.089111328125,
        401.74139404296875,
        545.3768920898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "#",
      "bbox": [
        401.7409362792969,
        524.1265258789062,
        407.54913330078125,
        530.5025634765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ",",
      "bbox": [
        409.21295166015625,
        534.6469116210938,
        411.9825439453125,
        543.4937133789062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(3)",
      "bbox": [
        493.0482177734375,
        534.8063354492188,
        504.6645812988281,
        543.712890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where x0 is a training sample, t is a continuous random variable drawn uniformly from [0, 1], xt is",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        562.31396484375,
        504.0004577636719,
        572.8739013671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sampled from the forward process and L is the sequence length. The indicator function 1[·] ensures",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        572.6650390625,
        504.0006408691406,
        582.2888793945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that the loss is computed only for masked tokens.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        584.2913818359375,
        304.55206298828125,
        593.1979370117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Once trained, we can simulate a reverse process (see Sec. 2.4 for details) parameterized by the mask",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        600.6793823242188,
        504.2485656738281,
        609.5859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "predictor and define the model distribution pθ(x0) as the marginal distribution induced at t = 0. The",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        611.429931640625,
        503.9972229003906,
        621.19091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "loss function in Eq. (3) has been proven to be an upper bound on the negative log-likelihood of the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        622.4983520507812,
        503.9981994628906,
        631.4049072265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model distribution, making it a principled objective for generative modeling:",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        633.4073486328125,
        413.0547180175781,
        642.3139038085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "−Epdata(x0) [log pθ(x0)] ≤L(θ).",
      "bbox": [
        242.39700317382812,
        650.0460815429688,
        369.6072692871094,
        661.3889770507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(4)",
      "bbox": [
        493.0638122558594,
        650.7633666992188,
        504.68017578125,
        659.669921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Notably, LLaDA employs a masking ratio that varies randomly between 0 and 1 while BERT [22]",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        673.599365234375,
        504.000244140625,
        682.5059204101562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uses a fixed ratio. The subtle differences have significant implications, especially at scale: as shown in",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        684.5083618164062,
        504.0014343261719,
        693.4149169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "6Here, we focus on the approach of LLaDA. A rigorous formulation of MDM is provided in Appendix A for",
      "bbox": [
        120.65299987792969,
        702.1752319335938,
        504.1529235839844,
        711.9737548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "interested readers.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        713.9207763671875,
        173.23056030273438,
        721.936767578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
